  "snippet": "#​671 — October 28, 2026 Web Version Postgres Weekly 'Region': A Lesson in Data Integrity — One of Lætitia's coworkers added a free-text region column and planned to validate it in app code, but Lætitia wouldn't approve ...",
  "coverImage": "https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/fjmq5nbgoygs2qyhpggn.jpg",
  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​671 — October 28, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192085/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb;\" target=\"_blank\">Web Version</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0 12px;\"><p>Postgres Weekly</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr style=\"line-height: 1.0em;\"><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.0em;\">\n<a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192052/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; line-height: 1.0em;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/fjmq5nbgoygs2qyhpggn.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 1.0em;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192052/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.4em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"mydbanotebook.org\">'Region': A Lesson in Data Integrity</a></span> — One of Lætitia's coworkers added a free-text <code>region</code> column and planned to validate it in app code, but Lætitia wouldn't approve it. Here she makes a case for keeping rules in the database with a look at domains, enums, <code>CHECK</code> constraints and lookup tables, and how to add constraints on large tables without blocking traffic.</p>\n<p>Lætitia Avrot </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192051/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"110\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/9dac2441.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"110\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192051/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.tigerdata.com\">CREATE INDEX on 100M Vectors in Under Two Hours</a></span> — HNSW indexes on large pgvector tables use lots of memory and can take days to build. Meet pg_vectorsearch: an open-source alternative for existing vector columns. At 100M vectors: a 25 GB index and 6 ms queries at 95% recall. <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192051/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb;\" target=\"_blank\">See the benchmarks</a>.</p>\n<p>Tiger Data (creators of TimescaleDB) <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><span>📖</span> <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192053/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"postgrespro.com\">PostgreSQL 18 Query Optimization: A Free 199-Page Book</a></span> — Postgres Pro's query tuning course, reshaped into a compact book that's now in English. It covers how the planner works, access methods, join strategies, statistics, reading execution plans and tuning approaches. <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192054/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb;\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the PDF</a>.</p>\n<p>Pavel Tolmachev (PostgresPro) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>IN BRIEF:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Microsoft <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192055/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">has started pitching SQL Server</a> to Postgres developers as an <em>'upgrade'</em>, touting its 32,767-connection limit. SQL Server expert <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192056/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Brent Ozar isn't buying it</a>, and Microsoft's author pops up in the comments to argue back.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🇺🇸 <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192057/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">PgDay Boston 2027</a> takes place on April 10, 2027 at Tufts University. <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192058/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Registration is open</a>, as is the <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192059/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">CFP</a> (until January 15).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🇺🇸 <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192060/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Postgres Day SF</a> is a free meetup (registration needs approval) at PlanetScale's San Francisco office on November 4, celebrating 30 years of Postgres with Bruce Momjian and Fabrizio Mello.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>📅 <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192061/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">POSETTE 2027</a>, Microsoft's annual virtual Postgres event, returns on March 30-31, 2027. No CFP yet.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192062/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"planetscale.com\">Why I Don't Trust <code>ON DELETE CASCADE</code></a></span> — One big cascading <code>DELETE</code> plus a routine migration can freeze writes to a table. Tom explains the lock queue behind it, some replication traps, and why he prefers soft deletes.</p>\n<p>Tom Pang (PlanetScale) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192063/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.photoroom.com\">How a Read Replica Almost Took Down Its Primary Database</a></span> — Google Cloud grows disks automatically so Photoroom wasn't worried about space. Then a backfill left a BI replica so far behind that the primary held 31.7TB of WAL for it. The disk grew close to a hard limit, and shrinking it meant downtime.</p>\n<p>Marek Zaremba-Pike (Photoroom) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192064/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.prisma.io\">Moving 74GB Off RDS with a Week-Long Rollback Window</a></span> — Prisma moved its console's database off RDS with logical replication and no write pause, then ran replication in <em>reverse</em> so it could fall back to RDS for a week.</p>\n<p>Siket and Datta (Prisma) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192065/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Your App Doesn't Need Postgres Superuser</a> – Superuser can run commands on the server, so here's what to grant apps and agents instead. <cite>Umair Shahid (Stormatics)</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192066/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Postgres 19 is Late, and It's AI's Fault</a> <cite>Robert Haas</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192067/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Tuning Postgres for Analytics</a> – Slides and transcript from PGConf.EU on running reports against your app's database without slowing it. <cite>Karen Jex</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>🎙️ Karen also joined Claire Giordano on the <em>Talking Postgres</em> podcast to talk about <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192068/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">her path from Oracle DBA to Postgres contributor</a>.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>⚡ <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192069/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Rebase</a> turns your Postgres into an API and an admin panel your team can use. Our own CRM: 23 tables, zero hand-written admin screens.</p>\n<p>⏱️ One 5-row lookup table turned a 0.3 ms Postgres query into 467 ms. <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192070/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Find yours before prod does</a>. Now in preview.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>RELEASES AND CODE:</strong></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr style=\"line-height: 1.0em;\"><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.0em;\">\n<a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192071/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; line-height: 1.0em;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/ey5jp6aqzwln1cm4yc4d.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 1.0em;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192071/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.pgedge.com\">pgVolvra: Flashback-Style 'Undo' for Bad <code>UPDATE</code>s and <code>DELETE</code>s</a></span> — Trigger-based row history that lets you preview and reverse a bad statement or migration by transaction ID. Plain SQL with no superuser needed, so it works on managed Postgres too. <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192072/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb;\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub repo</a>.</p>\n<p>Muhammad Aqeel (pgEdge) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192073/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"pgrust.com\">pgrust 0.4 Beta: The Rust Rewrite of Postgres Opens Up</a></span> — The experimental Rust reimplementation of Postgres adds a new JIT engine, transactional columnar tables and automatic memory sizing (no more <code>work_mem</code> tuning?).</p>\n<p>Michael Malis </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 ClickHouse <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192074/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">pulled pgrust from ClickBench</a> in September over per-query code and caching. With v0.4's source public, it's <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192075/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">back in</a>, and central to a <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192076/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">benchmark-overfitting debate</a>.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192077/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.pinecone.io\">pg_pinecone: Pinecone's Vector Index for pgvector Columns</a></span> — A new extension that indexes existing pgvector columns using IVF and RaBitQ quantization, applying filters during the search. Its native engine runs locally on Postgres 17 and 18, and Pinecone reports a 136MB index vs 2GB for HNSW on 1M vectors. <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192078/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb;\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub repo</a>.</p>\n<p>Daddala and Mahanna (Pinecone) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr style=\"line-height: 1.0em;\"><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.0em;\">\n<a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192079/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; line-height: 1.0em;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/yerrrdxckhvcxirfirjy.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 1.0em;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192079/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 1.08em; line-height: 1.5em;\" target=\"_blank\">pg_hdr_histogram 1.0</a> <em>(above)</em> – Store value distributions (e.g. latencies) as compact HDR histograms, then query p99-style percentiles and merge them losslessly across time windows or servers, say.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192080/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 1.08em; line-height: 1.5em;\" target=\"_blank\">mcdview</a> – Turn a Postgres schema dump (or a Prisma, pgModeler or Rails schema) into a searchable, shareable interactive ER diagram. You can <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192081/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">try it online</a> or see <a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192082/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">an example of its output here</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192083/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 1.08em; line-height: 1.5em;\" target=\"_blank\">Citus 14.3</a> – The distributed Postgres extension adds sorted-merge execution for multi-shard <code>ORDER BY</code> queries and per-shard pruning of <code>OR</code> clauses.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://postgresweekly.com/link/192084/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #0088bb; font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 1.08em; line-height: 1.5em;\" target=\"_blank\">SPQR 3.2</a> – Yandex's Postgres sharding router adds <code>spqrmigrate</code>, a schema migration tool.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
  "attachments": []
}